<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Container for the native ad card in Home's swipe stack
    (item_native_ad_card.xml).

    Mirrors bg_v2_card exactly - same fill, same 40dp radius, same hairline -
    so an ad and a profile read as the same kind of object in the same stack.
    It was bg_card, whose 16dp radius made the ad visibly squarer than every
    card around it after the swipe card moved to 40dp.

    A separate file rather than an edit to bg_card, which fourteen other
    layouts use: login, signup, payment, profile, the skeletons, and the ad
    GRID item, none of which should inherit a swipe-card radius.

    The stroke is load-bearing for the same reason bg_v2_card's is: at
    wedora_surface on wedora_bg the two tones are only about 1.3:1 apart, so
    without it the card has no edge in dark mode.

    MATCHING STOPS AT THE CONTAINER. Native ads are meant to match the host
    app's look and feel, and radius and border are exactly that. Giving this
    card the profile card's scrim, overlaid name line or like/pass controls
    would be a different thing - an ad structurally imitating a person, which
    is the "ad mimics content" line AdMob policy actually draws.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="rectangle">
    <solid android:color="@color/wedora_surface" />
    <corners android:radius="40dp" />
    <stroke
        android:width="1dp"
        android:color="@color/wedora_hairline" />
</shape>
